A||N||7||mbramble||PAINTING QUESTION||||1||
Z||000000||mbramble||03-02-2000||10:59 AM||||I will be putting my '87 Coupe in the shop in the near future for new paint.  What do I do about the trim??  The moulding, the 'rocker panel's beneath the doors, the vent covers over the battery, etc., trim on the sail panel.  Do these get painted or is there some other way to refresh them.  My original color is maroon (will have it repainted the same).  I can't tell if all that trim was black or a dark gray??<P>Any info would be most appreciated....<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||mbramble||03-02-2000||11:00 AM||||.....and -- the mirrors...<P>Mike<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||03-02-2000||11:11 AM||||Coupe's have black trim (rocker panels, moulding, mirrors, grills) and should stay that way. Don't let them paint over these nor the sail panel. That doesn't get painted at all. Preferably I wish my GT had black trim as well instead of previously being gray (ground effects), but I plan on painting them black in the near future.||||reg||2
Z||000003||mbramble||03-02-2000||11:23 AM||||Well, at least now I know it is supposed to be black.  Thanks.  It is so faded, it's hard to tell.  So, what do I do to make it black again -- have them paint it black or do something myself??<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||DRH||03-02-2000||12:59 PM||||Gokart is right to remain original. I have seen some pictures of cars that had the mirrors, grills, etc. painted to match the body. See the link below for an example. I think the body color mirrors give it a more modern look. Really just personal preference and how important being original is to you.<P> <A HREF="http://home.xnet.com/~paulv/88formul.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://home.xnet.com/~paulv/88formul.htm</A> <BR>||||reg||3
Z||000005||ChadMan||03-02-2000||02:17 PM||||Isn't Paul's Formula amazing?  I saw it at the Columbus show last August.  It is immaculate inside and out - plus it's got that V8 rumble.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phil||03-02-2000||03:10 PM||||I pulled off all the trim that I could before I sent it to the paint shop. The nylon clips that hold the side moldings on will most likely snap but they are only $1.50 ea from a dealer. I asked the guy at the paint shop what I should on the trim and moldings and he said just use trim paint. I got mine at Wal-Mart. There is even a brand that has a Fiero on the can||||reg||1
Z||000008||Gokart||03-02-2000||03:42 PM||||You'd be suprised how good the mirrors and grills will look if you just do them yourself with spray cans. Prep really well(sand,prime,etc) and use a semi-gloss or black enamel. If the paint shop offers to do them for a fair price, go for it, But if they want another arm or leg do it yourself!<p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 03-02-2000).]||||reg||10
